  "title": "Erdős Problem #683",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Is it true that for every $1\\leq k\\leq n$ the largest prime divisor of $\\binom{n}{k}$, say $P(\\binom{n}{k})$, satisfies $ P\\left(\\binom{n}{k}\\right)\\geq \\min(n-k+1, k^{1+c}) $ for some constant $c>0$?",
